1
00:00:10,635 --> 00:00:13,221
THAT DOCTOR IS A MONEY-GRUBBER,
A REAL SCAM ARTIST

2
00:00:14,806 --> 00:00:15,974
Oh, I'm sorry.

3
00:00:17,517 --> 00:00:18,476
Forgive me.

4
00:00:19,102 --> 00:00:20,186
I'll continue.

5
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:23,356
Once our Ginza branch
has opened next year,

6
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:25,900
Tohyama Clinic plans to expand nationwide,

7
00:00:25,984 --> 00:00:27,986
with new branches in Sapporo,

8
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:32,240
Kyoto, and Fukuoka by the year 2030.

9
00:00:34,826 --> 00:00:36,411
Any questions or concerns, people?

10
00:00:36,494 --> 00:00:37,912
Well…

11
00:00:38,663 --> 00:00:42,250
Forgive me, but I thought
you wanted to keep the practice small.

12
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:45,503
Not to mention,
has the chairman approved of this?

13
00:00:48,506 --> 00:00:50,175
His approval doesn't matter.

14
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,928
I run this clinic, not him.

15
00:00:54,012 --> 00:00:58,016
Turning a plastic surgery clinic
into a chain is a ridiculous concept.

16
00:00:58,725 --> 00:00:59,726
Do you know why?

17
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:06,232
It's because a chain could never guarantee
a Hand-of-God-level quality

18
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:10,612
that can be adapted
for each customer's individual needs.

19
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:18,453
How can you provide elite service
if you have to employ

20
00:01:18,536 --> 00:01:20,997
whatever mediocre doctors
you can get your hands on?

21
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:24,375
<i>Of course, I plan to hear out</i>
<i>any concerns the chairman might have.</i>

22
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:29,589
However, I've decided
that allowing him too much influence

23
00:01:29,672 --> 00:01:33,009
would only limit
the Tohyama Clinic's potential growth.

24
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:36,638
The concept of beauty
has evolved significantly

25
00:01:36,721 --> 00:01:40,475
since the chairman
was actively practicing as a surgeon.

26
00:01:41,142 --> 00:01:42,435
This clinic

27
00:01:43,561 --> 00:01:45,021
has to adapt or be left behind.

28
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:49,984
Cosmetic surgery
is the pinnacle of medicine.

29
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:53,488
The reason

30
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:57,784
is because we not only treat our patients,

31
00:01:58,576 --> 00:02:01,287
we also increase their social value.

32
00:02:02,539 --> 00:02:03,957
This can only be done

33
00:02:04,499 --> 00:02:09,003
by an exceptional surgeon
with a talent that's one-of-a-kind.

34
00:02:10,755 --> 00:02:12,090
I speak of myself.

35
00:02:12,173 --> 00:02:16,136
<i>The days of plastic surgery</i>
<i>being seen as a novelty are over.</i>

36
00:02:17,345 --> 00:02:20,598
Pretty soon, a visit to a cosmetic surgeon

37
00:02:21,099 --> 00:02:23,935
will be just as ordinary
as a trip to the dentist.

38
00:02:24,519 --> 00:02:25,562
It's only a matter of time.

39
00:02:25,645 --> 00:02:29,649
<i>The plastic surgery industry</i>
<i>is rife with charlatans.</i>

40
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:34,654
I find this to be… truly disturbing.

41
00:02:34,737 --> 00:02:36,072
SUCCESSOR OF THE HAND OF GOD

42
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:39,033
In the name of the Tohyama Surgery Clinic,

43
00:02:39,534 --> 00:02:43,580
I promise to unmask these medical frauds
and take them down.

44
00:02:52,714 --> 00:02:54,215
YOU GOT ANY PROOF, MS. COMPLAINER?

45
00:02:54,299 --> 00:02:56,801
YOU KNOW YOU COULD GET ARRESTED FOR THIS?

46
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:06,769
I HAVE A LAWYER TOO, YOU KNOW?
SHUT UP, FOOLS.

47
00:03:07,937 --> 00:03:11,441
Director, about Dr. Numata.

48
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:16,196
This was published today.

49
00:03:17,947 --> 00:03:19,616
It's an interview with Kana's mother.

50
00:03:23,161 --> 00:03:27,582
In the article,
she defends Dr. Numata's response.

51
00:03:29,667 --> 00:03:32,212
The nursing staff would like
to make a suggestion.

52
00:03:33,963 --> 00:03:36,299
Maybe the time has come

53
00:03:37,008 --> 00:03:39,385
for Dr. Numata to use her real name?

54
00:03:39,469 --> 00:03:42,347
Using an alias feels
like we're deceiving our patients.

55
00:03:42,430 --> 00:03:45,141
No. It's way too soon for that.

56
00:03:45,725 --> 00:03:49,270
And we don't even know
how many people read this magazine.

57
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:55,026
Numata, are you committed
to working as a plastic surgeon?

58
00:03:56,402 --> 00:03:59,239
I would also like to hear Numata's answer.

59
00:04:00,823 --> 00:04:04,869
Are you prepared
to use your medical skills

60
00:04:05,995 --> 00:04:08,331
to change people's appearances?

61
00:04:18,383 --> 00:04:19,300
The truth is that…

62
00:04:25,723 --> 00:04:27,141
I'd prefer to work

63
00:04:28,059 --> 00:04:28,893
under my name.

64
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:34,399
- I'm with you.
- Director.

65
00:04:34,482 --> 00:04:37,360
I understand your concerns, Dr. Rui.

66
00:04:37,443 --> 00:04:40,530
I don't want any blowback on us either.

67
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:43,908
I'll have our PR department investigate

68
00:04:43,992 --> 00:04:47,328
whether or not the heat
against Dr. Numata has subsided.

69
00:04:47,912 --> 00:04:50,331
I'll make my decision
after seeing the results.

70
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:51,541
'Kay.

71
00:05:04,971 --> 00:05:08,308
TAKERU NUMATA
CALL ME BACK NOW!

72
00:05:09,267 --> 00:05:10,435
What?

73
00:05:11,352 --> 00:05:13,021
MACKY, TAKASHI, HOME
MISSED CALLS

74
00:05:13,104 --> 00:05:14,856
What the…

75
00:05:14,939 --> 00:05:17,567
TAKERU NUMATA
MISSED CALL ONE HOUR AGO

76
00:05:30,496 --> 00:05:33,750
- Has the time been confirmed?
- Not yet. We're on standby.

77
00:05:34,625 --> 00:05:36,461
- Hey.
- What the hell happened?

78
00:05:37,795 --> 00:05:40,298
She was drinking this morning.
She fell and hit her head.

79
00:05:40,381 --> 00:05:41,758
What did the doctor say?

80
00:05:41,841 --> 00:05:45,011
A nurse said
she was gonna be taken into the ICU.

81
00:05:45,094 --> 00:05:47,472
- Did they really say the ICU?
- Yeah.

82
00:05:49,265 --> 00:05:50,808
Tojo, what's going on?

83
00:05:51,642 --> 00:05:54,896
She suffered a severe contusion,
and she's now having seizures.

84
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:57,857
- We'll do our best.
- I appreciate it.

85
00:06:01,027 --> 00:06:02,487
Wait, so what is it?

86
00:06:03,279 --> 00:06:05,073
I thought Mom had cirrhosis.

87
00:07:23,609 --> 00:07:24,902
Dr. Rui.

88
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:27,530
Are you ready for the next patient yet?

89
00:07:27,613 --> 00:07:30,032
Mm, give me another two minutes.

90
00:07:31,242 --> 00:07:34,162
Why do I have to be the one
to pick up Numata's slack?

91
00:07:34,662 --> 00:07:37,081
She has a family emergency.
Nothing to be done.

92
00:07:37,165 --> 00:07:39,709
By the way,
have you seen the recent blacklist?

93
00:07:39,792 --> 00:07:40,793
The blacklist?

94
00:07:41,961 --> 00:07:44,213
All the names of patients
who've filed complaints.

95
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:45,923
They published their real names?

96
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:46,924
Yes.

97
00:07:47,633 --> 00:07:49,844
Oh, this one here was a total psycho.

98
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:52,847
The second she walked in,
she started yelling at the staff,

99
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:54,682
and even hit the doctor. Ooh!

100
00:07:55,349 --> 00:07:57,935
- Whoa. Hey, can I take a picture?
- Sure.

101
00:07:58,686 --> 00:08:01,439
She then claimed
the whole experience traumatized her,

102
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:03,983
and she refused to pay for the treatment.

103
00:08:04,066 --> 00:08:07,445
Turns out all her claims
were made up entirely.

104
00:08:07,945 --> 00:08:10,781
- Talk about a pain in the ass.
- Mm.

105
00:08:15,912 --> 00:08:18,956
We should have done more
to stop her from drinking.

106
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:21,125
Should've tied her to a chair.

107
00:08:21,626 --> 00:08:23,794
She would have found a way
to keep on drinking.

108
00:08:23,878 --> 00:08:24,921
50% SURVIVAL RATE

109
00:08:25,004 --> 00:08:26,339
Seriously?

110
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:28,841
Here's the dermatologist's diagnosis.

111
00:08:31,093 --> 00:08:34,514
This can be used
as evidence in court, right?

112
00:08:35,014 --> 00:08:36,432
Yes, I don't see why not.

113
00:08:36,516 --> 00:08:38,518
You should have left the clinic
like Mom asked you.

114
00:08:40,394 --> 00:08:41,938
- What?
- I warned you, didn't I?

115
00:08:42,605 --> 00:08:46,025
Takeru, Fumi was only trying
to get rid of our debt.

116
00:08:46,108 --> 00:08:47,985
Mom was stressed out 'cause of it.

117
00:08:57,453 --> 00:09:00,706
SCULPTING THE PAST

118
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:02,750
How was your day at school?

119
00:09:02,833 --> 00:09:04,502
- Very good.
- What'd you do?

120
00:09:04,585 --> 00:09:06,629
Played with my friends. I played outside.

121
00:09:06,712 --> 00:09:08,005
Played some football. It was fun.

122
00:09:08,589 --> 00:09:11,425
You did a lot of playing.
Did you do anything else today?

123
00:09:11,509 --> 00:09:12,927
- Yeah.
- Okay.

124
00:09:13,010 --> 00:09:16,764
I GOT THE DIAGNOSIS! NOW I CAN GO AFTER
THE DOCTOR AND SEND HIM TO HELL.

125
00:09:16,847 --> 00:09:18,516
Uh, math. All that stuff.

126
00:09:18,599 --> 00:09:21,269
<i>Ms. Yuriko Sakashita,</i>
<i>who caught the public eye</i>

127
00:09:21,352 --> 00:09:24,188
<i>after undergoing</i>
<i>a full-body surgical transformation,</i>

128
00:09:24,272 --> 00:09:25,982
<i>despite having terminal cancer,</i>

129
00:09:26,065 --> 00:09:28,484
<i>is reported</i>
<i>to have passed away last night.</i>

130
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:30,278
<i>She was 75.</i>

131
00:09:30,361 --> 00:09:32,572
<i>The procedure was filmed</i>
<i>for a documentary,</i>

132
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:35,825
<i>which includes an interview</i>
<i>from her surgeon, Dr. Rin Tohyama</i>

133
00:09:35,908 --> 00:09:38,411
<i>at the Tohyama Cosmetic Surgery Clinic.</i>

134
00:09:38,911 --> 00:09:43,624
<i>According to her family, Ms. Sakashita</i>
<i>professed her sincerest gratitude to you</i>

135
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:45,960
<i>just moments before she passed away.</i>

136
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:48,713
<i>It was because of Ms. Yuriko's courage</i>

137
00:09:50,339 --> 00:09:52,216
<i>that I was able to deliver such results.</i>

138
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:56,178
<i>This was all possible because of her.</i>

139
00:09:56,679 --> 00:10:00,224
- I suppose it runs in the family.
<i>- We've received comments from viewers.</i>

140
00:10:01,225 --> 00:10:03,352
I've heard
this documentary she was filming

141
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:05,688
is being adapted into a drama.

142
00:10:06,772 --> 00:10:08,524
What could have been
such a publicity stunt

143
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:11,444
was instead
turned into a pretty moving story.

144
00:10:12,028 --> 00:10:13,654
Worthy of the Hand of God.

145
00:10:14,155 --> 00:10:15,990
<i>…must have been so encouraging to…</i>

146
00:10:16,073 --> 00:10:19,118
By the way, looks like the Ginza property
we were interested in

147
00:10:19,201 --> 00:10:20,661
was snatched up by someone else.

148
00:10:20,745 --> 00:10:22,246
<i>Watching Ms. Yuriko…</i>

149
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:24,165
The realtor just called to say that.

150
00:10:24,915 --> 00:10:27,835
Hmm. That's unfortunate.

151
00:10:28,794 --> 00:10:30,963
That location was perfect.

152
00:10:31,797 --> 00:10:35,134
Maybe there's room to negotiate?

153
00:10:35,217 --> 00:10:36,427
Not sure.

154
00:10:37,094 --> 00:10:39,263
They're in the same business as us.

155
00:10:40,097 --> 00:10:43,225
Well,
all the more reason to try to get it.

156
00:10:43,726 --> 00:10:44,560
<i>This case…</i>

157
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:45,895
Who is it?

158
00:10:45,978 --> 00:10:48,105
<i>…was inspiring for me too.</i>

159
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:51,651
Because of her resiliency.

160
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:53,861
Are you sure

161
00:10:55,488 --> 00:10:57,823
you don't wanna unmask these frauds
once and for all?

162
00:11:46,706 --> 00:11:49,417
Oh, Elsa. Are you healed already?

163
00:11:49,917 --> 00:11:52,211
Still swollen,
but no one will notice in this lighting.

164
00:11:52,795 --> 00:11:54,171
You're right.

165
00:11:54,255 --> 00:11:57,007
At this point,
you're indistinguishable from the poster.

166
00:11:58,008 --> 00:12:00,678
I got so tired of the filter accusations.

167
00:12:04,473 --> 00:12:06,016
Hi, I'm Elsa.

168
00:12:06,892 --> 00:12:08,894
Wait. Yama, is that you?

169
00:12:08,978 --> 00:12:11,063
I haven't seen you in ages.

170
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:13,816
I'm sorry.
I hear you've been requesting me.

171
00:12:14,316 --> 00:12:17,069
You were gone for so long,
I was worried you'd quit.

172
00:12:19,530 --> 00:12:21,866
Wow, you're lovelier than ever.

173
00:12:24,368 --> 00:12:26,120
Thanks.

174
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:30,666
Oh. What's this?

175
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:33,753
Happy birthday, Elsa.

176
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:35,337
Huh?

177
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:38,340
Please enjoy this premium champagne
and this cake

178
00:12:38,424 --> 00:12:40,968
courtesy of Ms. Elsa's wonderful client.

179
00:12:41,051 --> 00:12:43,012
What? You really did this?

180
00:12:43,095 --> 00:12:44,346
Oh, that's so nice!

181
00:12:45,431 --> 00:12:46,766
Happy birthday.

182
00:12:46,849 --> 00:12:48,726
Oh, thank you. This is wonderful, wow.

183
00:12:48,809 --> 00:12:51,103
Look at all this. Thank you so much.

184
00:12:51,187 --> 00:12:53,731
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

185
00:12:53,814 --> 00:12:57,485
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

186
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:13,459
- She made it through.
- Thank you.

187
00:13:14,502 --> 00:13:16,587
Oh, wow. Thank goodness.

188
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:18,047
Thank you, Doctor.

189
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:21,300
Is my mom awake?

190
00:13:21,383 --> 00:13:23,969
Not yet.
She's asleep from the anesthesia still.

191
00:13:24,053 --> 00:13:26,764
I think it's best
to wait until tomorrow to see her.

192
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:29,600
Before you go, a word?

193
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:31,185
Mm-hmm.

194
00:13:45,699 --> 00:13:47,451
Must bring back memories, huh?

195
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:50,538
First time this room has been used
by both parent and child.

196
00:13:50,621 --> 00:13:51,872
How did it go?

197
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:56,418
She was bleeding heavily.

198
00:13:57,169 --> 00:13:58,712
It was worse than I thought.

199
00:13:58,796 --> 00:13:59,964
I see.

200
00:14:00,047 --> 00:14:02,591
Even if she does wake up,
there is a high chance

201
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:04,969
that she'll be left
with significant cognitive impairment.

202
00:14:05,052 --> 00:14:06,053
Mm.

203
00:14:08,138 --> 00:14:09,223
Even so,

204
00:14:11,016 --> 00:14:13,561
she'll keep causing us trouble
for a long time still.

205
00:14:20,776 --> 00:14:23,195
Four clinics at the same time. Four!

206
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:27,449
That means there's openings
for all of us to be director.

207
00:14:28,158 --> 00:14:31,787
But there's four clinics and three of us,
so that leaves one spot open.

208
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:32,830
Numata?

209
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:35,749
No, no way. Not a chance.
She'd never get it.

210
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:37,626
Sorry to have kept you all waiting.

211
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:39,461
- Hey, everyone.
- Hi.

212
00:14:40,045 --> 00:14:44,174
We were all ready to head out
when a pretty nasty case walked in.

213
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:45,301
Nasty?

214
00:14:45,801 --> 00:14:48,470
Ah, it was someone from the blacklist.

215
00:14:48,554 --> 00:14:50,931
- Really?
- Yeah, same name and same face.

216
00:14:51,015 --> 00:14:51,974
That's right.

217
00:14:52,057 --> 00:14:54,560
Dr. Rui, you're definitely gonna want
to refuse her service.

218
00:14:54,643 --> 00:14:56,979
Oh no! Why do I have to deal with her?

219
00:14:57,062 --> 00:14:58,647
That's the director's job, isn't it?

220
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:03,569
Well, the director has a special
VIP client tomorrow at the clinic.

221
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:05,779
- Mm.
- Will you all have the table d'hôte too?

222
00:15:06,614 --> 00:15:07,489
Oh.

223
00:15:08,115 --> 00:15:10,200
Oh. Don't worry.

224
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:13,037
I've got the best weight-loss drug
on the market.

225
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:16,415
- Oh, well, in that case, let's eat!
- Yeah, let's eat!

226
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:31,221
I GOT THE DIAGNOSIS!

227
00:15:31,972 --> 00:15:33,766
LOOKING FORWARD TO UPDATES.

228
00:15:33,849 --> 00:15:35,643
NICE FORGERY. HOW CHILDISH OF YOU.

229
00:15:36,769 --> 00:15:38,395
Who do they think they are?

230
00:15:41,982 --> 00:15:43,609
OF COURSE IT'S NOT FABRICATED.

231
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:49,114
THAT CLINIC IS DONE FOR
AND SO ARE YOU, STOOGE.

232
00:15:52,952 --> 00:15:54,870
- <i>Yay! I win!</i>
- <i>One more time, Mommy!</i>

233
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:57,706
Mommy can't, sweetheart.
She'll be late to the club.

234
00:15:57,790 --> 00:16:01,210
- I've gotta go.
- Please! Can we play again?

235
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:02,211
Please, Mom?

236
00:16:02,294 --> 00:16:05,047
Oh, fine. Just one more time, okay?

237
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:06,173
Yes!

238
00:16:06,256 --> 00:16:09,927
Anyway, you know
that Mommy always wins, don't I?

239
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:11,720
This time, I'm gonna win for sure.

240
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:15,724
How many times have I heard you say that?

241
00:16:16,225 --> 00:16:18,477
Okay, hurry. Let's go!

242
00:16:26,902 --> 00:16:27,861
Mom.

243
00:16:28,362 --> 00:16:29,446
Are you awake?

244
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:35,619
I'm in trouble.

245
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:37,329
What's wrong?

246
00:16:38,330 --> 00:16:40,165
Can I…

247
00:16:42,167 --> 00:16:43,585
borrow your phone?

248
00:16:46,797 --> 00:16:48,507
My Fumi,

249
00:16:49,675 --> 00:16:51,343
she must be so worried.

250
00:16:51,927 --> 00:16:53,053
But, Mom.

251
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:54,805
Mom, it's me.

252
00:16:54,888 --> 00:16:56,515
Fumi's only

253
00:16:57,683 --> 00:16:59,351
in fourth grade.

254
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:01,437
She's…

255
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:02,521
Mm.

256
00:17:03,022 --> 00:17:04,481
- …home alone…
- Don't worry.

257
00:17:04,565 --> 00:17:06,442
- I'm sure she's fine.
- …instead of here.

258
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:07,359
It'll be fine.

259
00:17:08,527 --> 00:17:10,237
- Your phone.
- It's okay.

260
00:17:10,738 --> 00:17:11,989
Can I use it?

261
00:17:13,699 --> 00:17:15,117
Can you tell me your name?

262
00:17:15,617 --> 00:17:16,785
She has memory loss?

263
00:17:16,869 --> 00:17:18,746
Yeah, I'm afraid she does,

264
00:17:18,829 --> 00:17:20,914
but it's common
after a subarachnoid hemorrhage.

265
00:17:20,998 --> 00:17:22,082
When's your birthday?

266
00:17:22,166 --> 00:17:24,251
Though the memory
usually comes back with rehab.

267
00:17:24,334 --> 00:17:25,169
I see.

268
00:17:25,252 --> 00:17:26,462
October 4th.

269
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:29,048
Do you know where you are?

270
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:30,632
Mom, it's me.

271
00:17:36,972 --> 00:17:38,140
Takeru.

272
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:43,062
A specialist is going to treat
her memory loss.

273
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:45,856
Okay? Don't worry.

274
00:17:48,859 --> 00:17:50,861
We should go. Hmm?

275
00:17:51,904 --> 00:17:53,197
I gotta go to work.

276
00:17:54,239 --> 00:17:55,365
Look after her.

277
00:17:58,494 --> 00:18:01,747
Doctor, I've uploaded
today's intake forms.

278
00:18:01,830 --> 00:18:02,664
DR. TANUMA

279
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:04,333
Great, thanks.

280
00:18:04,958 --> 00:18:06,001
Good morning.

281
00:18:06,585 --> 00:18:08,504
- Morning.
- I'm sorry about your mother.

282
00:18:09,463 --> 00:18:11,006
Thanks. She's out of the woods.

283
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:14,551
Oh. I hear you'll be handling
the counseling sessions today.

284
00:18:14,635 --> 00:18:15,511
A word of advice.

285
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:18,597
Don't start the conversation with a no.

286
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:20,557
You have a tendency to do that.

287
00:18:21,391 --> 00:18:24,019
And smile, okay?

288
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:25,854
Yeah.

289
00:18:35,656 --> 00:18:37,074
Come in.

290
00:18:37,157 --> 00:18:40,869
Excuse me, Dr. Tanuma,
your patient has arrived.

291
00:18:43,705 --> 00:18:46,083
I'm Dr. Tanuma. It's nice to meet you.

292
00:18:46,166 --> 00:18:47,251
Nice to meet you.

293
00:18:47,334 --> 00:18:49,294
You can place your belongings here.

294
00:18:55,175 --> 00:18:57,845
- Governor, welcome to my clinic.
- We've been expecting you.

295
00:18:57,928 --> 00:19:00,597
Dr. Rin, it's been a while.

296
00:19:03,225 --> 00:19:06,520
So tell me, Ms. Itai,
what would you like to focus on?

297
00:19:07,437 --> 00:19:11,275
Uh, the buccal fat under my cheekbones.

298
00:19:11,358 --> 00:19:13,360
It's starting to sag,
and I'd like to fix it.

299
00:19:13,443 --> 00:19:15,821
I don't like my philtrum very much either.

300
00:19:15,904 --> 00:19:17,197
I think it's too long.

301
00:19:17,281 --> 00:19:19,950
I know it's not that huge of an issue,
I guess,

302
00:19:20,033 --> 00:19:22,661
but I think that maybe
lifting the cheekbones here

303
00:19:22,744 --> 00:19:25,122
will make my philtrum look a lot shorter.

304
00:19:27,624 --> 00:19:28,458
Okay.

305
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:30,335
A Global Beauty Hub?

306
00:19:30,419 --> 00:19:31,837
Yes.

307
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:35,215
Plastic surgery is booming in popularity,
wouldn't you say?

308
00:19:35,299 --> 00:19:38,177
Japanese doctors
are renowned for their skill.

309
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:42,306
So, I want to promote the idea

310
00:19:42,389 --> 00:19:46,310
of Tokyo as the world capital of beauty.

311
00:19:47,144 --> 00:19:48,979
That's an amazing idea.

312
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:53,108
So, is this for the upcoming election?

313
00:19:53,192 --> 00:19:57,404
Yes. I think it'll become
a major campaign talking point.

314
00:19:57,487 --> 00:19:59,865
That will certainly appeal
to the female vote.

315
00:19:59,948 --> 00:20:04,494
And I would like
the face of this new campaign to be

316
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:08,624
my favorite doctor in the entire industry.

317
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:10,584
Okay?

318
00:20:11,376 --> 00:20:12,461
What?

319
00:20:12,544 --> 00:20:14,004
You willing to help us out?

320
00:20:19,718 --> 00:20:20,886
Of course I will.

321
00:20:21,803 --> 00:20:23,513
I'll be more than happy to help you.

322
00:20:25,724 --> 00:20:28,393
Uh, do you mind if I ask you a question?

323
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:29,436
Of course.

324
00:20:29,519 --> 00:20:30,812
Thanks.

325
00:20:30,896 --> 00:20:36,443
Um, I see that you had surgery
on your upper lip not long ago, right?

326
00:20:37,486 --> 00:20:38,403
Oh.

327
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:41,448
No, I've been going to a new dentist,

328
00:20:41,531 --> 00:20:44,409
but the guy has no idea
how to properly inject Novocain.

329
00:20:45,452 --> 00:20:48,789
So the last surgery you had was...

330
00:20:49,414 --> 00:20:51,375
I think it was over a year ago.

331
00:20:51,458 --> 00:20:52,918
Posterior liposuction.

332
00:20:53,794 --> 00:20:54,711
Mm.

333
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:59,716
Um, in my professional opinion, Ms. Itai,

334
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:02,594
you've had
a rather large number of surgeries.

335
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:04,263
And as a result,

336
00:21:04,346 --> 00:21:07,224
the overall balance of your face
has altered.

337
00:21:07,307 --> 00:21:08,350
Oh, okay.

338
00:21:08,433 --> 00:21:09,935
We could shorten your philtrum,

339
00:21:10,018 --> 00:21:12,312
but it might upset the balance
now that your chin--

340
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:14,523
But the balance is off right now.
That's the problem.

341
00:21:14,606 --> 00:21:16,358
But before you shorten your philtrum--

342
00:21:16,441 --> 00:21:18,944
I'm the one
who has to live with this face, not you.

343
00:21:21,989 --> 00:21:23,699
I know better than you what my face needs.

344
00:21:27,536 --> 00:21:28,453
Okay.

345
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:31,665
You're right.

346
00:21:31,748 --> 00:21:34,668
Well, the office
will be in touch with details.

347
00:21:34,751 --> 00:21:35,752
Great.

348
00:21:35,836 --> 00:21:37,629
I will do everything I can.

349
00:21:37,713 --> 00:21:39,172
Excited to help.

350
00:21:39,256 --> 00:21:40,549
Sounds great.

351
00:21:41,341 --> 00:21:44,553
So can you fill in Chairman Tohyama
about everything?

352
00:21:46,013 --> 00:21:46,930
Sorry?

353
00:21:47,014 --> 00:21:50,350
Well, can't begin
without our Hand of God, can we?

354
00:21:50,434 --> 00:21:53,061
Both father and daughter
will be the faces of our campaign.

355
00:21:55,355 --> 00:21:57,649
Yes. I'll fill him in on everything.

356
00:21:57,733 --> 00:21:59,484
- Yes, please do.
- Yes.

357
00:21:59,568 --> 00:22:00,444
Great.

358
00:22:04,239 --> 00:22:05,115
Great seeing you.

359
00:22:11,496 --> 00:22:13,206
<i>I'm Denno. I'm the chief counselor.</i>

360
00:22:13,790 --> 00:22:16,001
If you don't mind, let's discuss payment.

361
00:22:17,252 --> 00:22:19,963
Doctor, I'll take it from here.

362
00:22:20,047 --> 00:22:20,964
Oh.

363
00:22:23,008 --> 00:22:24,051
Excuse me.

364
00:22:27,512 --> 00:22:29,473
Well then, shall we see?

365
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:36,396
Uh, right. Why don't I walk you through
the next steps, then?

366
00:22:42,361 --> 00:22:44,488
DAD

367
00:22:59,961 --> 00:23:01,588
Director, do you have a minute?

368
00:23:01,671 --> 00:23:04,508
Bad news. That patient we just talked to…

369
00:23:04,591 --> 00:23:06,843
Turns out she's on the blacklist.

370
00:23:08,053 --> 00:23:11,306
I'm so sorry. I should have checked
when she booked.

371
00:23:11,390 --> 00:23:13,934
Has her surgery already been scheduled?

372
00:23:14,017 --> 00:23:16,311
- Yes, in two days.
- You gotta be kidding.

373
00:23:16,395 --> 00:23:18,688
I know this isn't really my place to say,

374
00:23:18,772 --> 00:23:21,024
but this patient is still recovering
from her last surgery.

375
00:23:21,108 --> 00:23:23,443
- What?
- That's not right.

376
00:23:23,527 --> 00:23:25,362
Yeah, but I thought--

377
00:23:25,445 --> 00:23:27,489
This is going too far now.

378
00:23:27,572 --> 00:23:29,366
Think about it, Numata.

379
00:23:29,449 --> 00:23:31,451
She's filed complaints
at multiple clinics.

380
00:23:31,535 --> 00:23:33,787
I think she has body dysmorphia

381
00:23:34,287 --> 00:23:36,581
or even an addiction to plastic surgery.

382
00:23:37,082 --> 00:23:38,250
Has she paid in full?

383
00:23:38,333 --> 00:23:40,710
She applied for a loan,
but didn't qualify.

384
00:23:41,211 --> 00:23:45,382
But she insists she can find the cash
to pay upfront if she has to.

385
00:23:47,217 --> 00:23:50,303
Look, I'll call her
and talk to her about it.

386
00:24:08,947 --> 00:24:09,781
Yes?

387
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:12,909
Good morning. Am I speaking to Ms. Itai?

388
00:24:13,410 --> 00:24:15,996
This is Tanuma
calling from the Tohyama Clinic.

389
00:24:16,955 --> 00:24:18,582
Do you have a moment to chat?

390
00:24:19,749 --> 00:24:21,501
I'm at work, so make it quick.

391
00:24:21,585 --> 00:24:23,170
Yes, yes, of course.

392
00:24:23,253 --> 00:24:28,508
Uh, I'd like to talk to you
about your loan application.

393
00:24:28,592 --> 00:24:31,678
<i>It looks like it wasn't approved,</i>
<i>so according to the clinic's policy--</i>

394
00:24:31,761 --> 00:24:33,972
I said I'd pay cash
if the loan didn't go through.

395
00:24:34,055 --> 00:24:34,973
Right.

396
00:24:35,056 --> 00:24:38,268
But the thing is, according to our policy,

397
00:24:38,351 --> 00:24:42,606
we can't approve surgery for patients
whose loan applications are denied.

398
00:24:42,689 --> 00:24:45,484
What? That's ridiculous.
I have never heard of that.

399
00:24:45,567 --> 00:24:48,653
Do you make everyone who wants to pay cash
apply for a loan?

400
00:24:48,737 --> 00:24:51,281
N… No, we don't, but in your case--

401
00:24:51,364 --> 00:24:53,074
Are you denying me treatment?

402
00:24:53,158 --> 00:24:55,744
I'm recording this call, you know.
I'll sue you.

403
00:24:55,827 --> 00:24:58,955
Um, Ms. Itai,
I might be overstepping here,

404
00:24:59,039 --> 00:25:02,834
but would you come in
for another counseling session?

405
00:25:03,376 --> 00:25:05,504
<i>- Because last time--</i>
- I've got work. I can't talk.

406
00:25:05,587 --> 00:25:07,088
<i>Wait, Ms. Itai, don't go yet--</i>

407
00:25:07,923 --> 00:25:08,924
Damn it!

408
00:25:09,591 --> 00:25:10,634
Shit!

409
00:25:23,313 --> 00:25:25,190
I thought I made myself clear.

410
00:25:25,273 --> 00:25:27,067
You were supposed to get rid of her
for good.

411
00:25:27,150 --> 00:25:30,278
I know, but Ms. Itai won't listen to me.

412
00:25:30,362 --> 00:25:34,491
There's no benefit for our clinic
in doing surgery on someone like her.

413
00:25:35,075 --> 00:25:37,702
You need to take this more seriously.
This is not good for us.

414
00:25:37,786 --> 00:25:41,373
Is that… really my responsibility?

415
00:25:41,456 --> 00:25:42,832
Of course it is.

416
00:25:43,500 --> 00:25:45,752
Proper communication with patients

417
00:25:45,835 --> 00:25:49,214
is one of the most important parts
of being a surgeon.

418
00:25:50,006 --> 00:25:51,800
If you don't get that,

419
00:25:51,883 --> 00:25:54,553
then I definitely can't allow you
to work under your real name.

420
00:25:58,223 --> 00:25:59,474
Okay, I'll speak with her.

421
00:26:05,981 --> 00:26:07,566
- Takashina.
- Yes?

422
00:26:09,943 --> 00:26:11,278
Look into this person for me.

423
00:26:13,280 --> 00:26:14,990
All right.

424
00:26:18,785 --> 00:26:21,621
Ah. Thanks again for seeing me today.

425
00:26:22,581 --> 00:26:25,083
<i>Of course. And thank you as well.</i>

426
00:26:25,875 --> 00:26:29,170
<i>So, about your Beauty Hub project.</i>

427
00:26:29,921 --> 00:26:31,923
<i>I just heard back from the chairman.</i>

428
00:26:32,841 --> 00:26:33,675
Excellent.

429
00:26:34,426 --> 00:26:35,719
<i>What did he say?</i>

430
00:26:36,428 --> 00:26:38,054
He regretfully declined.

431
00:26:39,347 --> 00:26:41,933
But he sends his sincerest apologies.

432
00:26:42,976 --> 00:26:44,769
He's confident I can handle it on my own.

433
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:51,651
So now this patient
is completely ghosting you.

434
00:26:52,152 --> 00:26:54,195
She won't answer any of my calls.

435
00:26:54,946 --> 00:26:56,865
What am I supposed to do now?

436
00:26:57,365 --> 00:26:59,784
So she's addicted to plastic surgery.

437
00:26:59,868 --> 00:27:03,204
I can see how
the clinic would see her as a liability.

438
00:27:03,955 --> 00:27:06,124
Still, I hope you don't give up on her.

439
00:27:07,208 --> 00:27:08,752
- Really?
- Yeah.

440
00:27:08,835 --> 00:27:10,462
I think I'm also addicted.

441
00:27:11,921 --> 00:27:13,548
Mm, more importantly,

442
00:27:13,632 --> 00:27:16,509
the backlash against you
is gaining traction again.

443
00:27:16,593 --> 00:27:17,552
You mean…

444
00:27:17,636 --> 00:27:20,930
I know. I was surprised to see it too.

445
00:27:21,890 --> 00:27:22,724
Look.

446
00:27:22,807 --> 00:27:24,267
FUMI NUMATA IS STILL A DOCTOR

447
00:27:24,351 --> 00:27:26,311
SHE SWITCHED TO A COSMETIC CLINIC?

448
00:27:26,394 --> 00:27:27,896
Oh, come on.

449
00:27:27,979 --> 00:27:30,023
This again?

450
00:27:30,106 --> 00:27:32,400
I thought the interview
with Kanabun's mother

451
00:27:32,484 --> 00:27:33,943
would calm things down a bit.

452
00:27:34,527 --> 00:27:38,448
Hey, you think someone
could be adding fuel to the fire?

453
00:27:38,531 --> 00:27:39,824
What for? What do you mean?

454
00:27:39,908 --> 00:27:41,451
Girl, I don't know.

455
00:27:42,369 --> 00:27:44,663
- Want me to investigate?
- Can you?

456
00:27:48,583 --> 00:27:49,876
I gotta pay for it?

457
00:27:51,169 --> 00:27:52,128
Sorry, yeah.

458
00:27:52,212 --> 00:27:54,422
I gotta pay for my osteotomy next month.

459
00:27:54,506 --> 00:27:55,715
Mm, fine.

460
00:27:56,383 --> 00:27:57,926
- Let's do it.
- You can count on me.

461
00:27:59,052 --> 00:28:01,137
- An advance?
- I'm sorry.

462
00:28:01,221 --> 00:28:03,390
I wouldn't ask if I didn't really need it.

463
00:28:03,473 --> 00:28:05,642
More plastic surgery?

464
00:28:06,643 --> 00:28:09,020
If you want,
I can get you work at a brothel.

465
00:28:09,104 --> 00:28:10,146
You'll make more money.

466
00:28:15,151 --> 00:28:18,071
But that face wouldn't look so great
in bright lighting, would it?

467
00:28:20,699 --> 00:28:23,076
Here. You ready?

468
00:28:23,159 --> 00:28:23,993
Ah.

469
00:28:25,328 --> 00:28:26,287
There.

470
00:28:26,996 --> 00:28:28,206
Oh. Ah!

471
00:28:30,208 --> 00:28:31,376
Here.

472
00:28:31,459 --> 00:28:33,628
Yeah!

473
00:28:33,712 --> 00:28:35,255
Sorry, Takeru.

474
00:28:35,755 --> 00:28:37,465
- You lose.
- Yeah, you lose!

475
00:28:37,549 --> 00:28:38,466
Suck it, Takeru.

476
00:28:38,550 --> 00:28:39,801
Mom, is your memory back?

477
00:28:42,554 --> 00:28:43,513
Oh.

478
00:28:44,389 --> 00:28:45,724
It's you again.

479
00:28:46,307 --> 00:28:47,642
From the other day.

480
00:28:48,643 --> 00:28:52,814
Would you like… to play cards with us?

481
00:28:54,649 --> 00:28:56,025
Yeah, play with us.

482
00:28:57,527 --> 00:28:58,361
No, thanks.

483
00:28:58,445 --> 00:28:59,571
- Come on, join us!
- Why?

484
00:28:59,654 --> 00:29:01,865
- I'm good.
- The more the merrier, right?

485
00:29:01,948 --> 00:29:03,408
- Right.
- Tell her.

486
00:29:03,491 --> 00:29:04,659
I'll deal. Here we go.

487
00:29:06,411 --> 00:29:07,412
Takeru?

488
00:29:08,496 --> 00:29:09,998
Yeah, just one more time.

489
00:29:11,291 --> 00:29:12,876
What's going on with Mom?

490
00:29:13,418 --> 00:29:17,213
Oh. Apparently, she once dated someone
who looks exactly like Macky.

491
00:29:17,297 --> 00:29:18,256
Really?

492
00:29:18,339 --> 00:29:20,633
Isn't that right, Ms. Taeko?

493
00:29:20,717 --> 00:29:21,551
Mmm.

494
00:29:21,634 --> 00:29:24,262
I guess I look like someone
she knew in school.

495
00:29:25,013 --> 00:29:26,473
Love at first sight.

496
00:29:27,056 --> 00:29:28,808
Right?

497
00:29:28,892 --> 00:29:29,976
That's right.

498
00:29:32,854 --> 00:29:34,272
Hang on, stop!

499
00:29:35,190 --> 00:29:37,859
Come on, knock it off, Takeru.
You don't wanna see this.

500
00:29:39,110 --> 00:29:40,195
- Ha!
- Hey!

501
00:29:40,278 --> 00:29:42,697
- Aha!
- Hey, that's no fair!

502
00:29:43,656 --> 00:29:45,867
Ms. Taeko, you're last.

503
00:29:48,286 --> 00:29:50,288
- Better luck next time.
- Right.

504
00:29:50,371 --> 00:29:51,915
- Let's try again.
- Yeah.

505
00:29:51,998 --> 00:29:53,708
You'll win the next one for sure.

506
00:29:54,292 --> 00:29:56,085
- There you are.
- Thank you.

507
00:29:57,670 --> 00:29:59,088
Hey, Yama.

508
00:30:07,639 --> 00:30:08,473
You mean that?

509
00:30:17,690 --> 00:30:19,567
72-HOUR EMERGENCY CONTRACEPTIVE

510
00:30:42,590 --> 00:30:43,466
Yes?

511
00:30:43,550 --> 00:30:46,386
<i>Hi. It's me. This a good time?</i>

512
00:30:48,012 --> 00:30:49,013
Mm-hmm.

513
00:30:49,764 --> 00:30:51,724
<i>Are you coming to Tomoki's game?</i>

514
00:30:52,851 --> 00:30:54,394
<i>'Cause my parents will be there,</i>

515
00:30:54,477 --> 00:30:57,772
<i>and I really don't want another scene</i>
<i>like last time, understood?</i>

516
00:30:59,357 --> 00:31:00,650
But I was…

517
00:31:12,787 --> 00:31:14,122
I did this.

518
00:31:14,205 --> 00:31:15,248
It's my fault.

519
00:31:15,331 --> 00:31:16,374
Hey.

520
00:31:17,500 --> 00:31:20,295
I'm such an idiot. That's why he…

521
00:31:20,378 --> 00:31:21,296
Mom?

522
00:31:22,672 --> 00:31:24,716
That's why he left. It's all my fault.

523
00:31:26,843 --> 00:31:29,429
It's okay, Mom. It's okay. What is it?

524
00:31:30,096 --> 00:31:31,848
He left me with Fumi.

525
00:31:34,309 --> 00:31:35,393
What?

526
00:31:39,731 --> 00:31:41,482
<i>I'm going to his game, you hear me?</i>

527
00:31:42,650 --> 00:31:46,321
I've been looking forward to this
for so long.

528
00:31:47,196 --> 00:31:49,574
And I promised Tomo that I would be there!

529
00:31:49,657 --> 00:31:51,409
I have to be there.

530
00:31:51,492 --> 00:31:53,536
<i>He doesn't remember</i>
<i>you making that promise.</i>

531
00:31:53,620 --> 00:31:55,204
I'm allowed to see him!

532
00:31:55,288 --> 00:31:57,248
I have visitation rights, you know!

533
00:31:57,332 --> 00:32:00,668
I don't care what your parents think.
It's none of their business!

534
00:32:01,377 --> 00:32:04,964
If you try to stop me from seeing my son,
I'll call my lawyer!

535
00:32:10,345 --> 00:32:12,013
<i>It's my fault.</i>

536
00:32:13,848 --> 00:32:16,100
- It's all my fault.
- Mm. Mom.

537
00:32:16,184 --> 00:32:19,103
Please forgive me, Fumi.

538
00:32:19,187 --> 00:32:20,772
It's okay. You're okay.

539
00:32:21,272 --> 00:32:23,232
- I'm so sorry.
- It's okay.

540
00:32:23,316 --> 00:32:24,150
Hey, Mom.

541
00:32:24,776 --> 00:32:25,735
You're fine.

542
00:32:27,362 --> 00:32:31,574
I need to ask a favor of you.

543
00:32:31,658 --> 00:32:33,284
Mm-hmm. What is it?

544
00:32:33,368 --> 00:32:35,620
I really need some alcohol.

545
00:32:38,623 --> 00:32:39,791
I'm sorry, no.

546
00:32:40,750 --> 00:32:43,086
- If you drink again, you'll die.
- I need it.

547
00:32:43,169 --> 00:32:44,754
- No, I'm sorry.
- I can't take it anymore.

548
00:32:44,837 --> 00:32:47,882
I can get you a glass of water.
Just have some water, take a breath.

549
00:32:47,966 --> 00:32:49,133
- Okay?
- Fine.

550
00:32:49,842 --> 00:32:52,220
- I'll get some myself.
- No, Mom. Stop.

551
00:32:52,303 --> 00:32:55,098
Mom, calm down.
Mom, stop! You'll pull out your IV!

552
00:32:55,932 --> 00:32:58,351
- Let me go!
- Mom! Mom, calm down!

553
00:32:59,143 --> 00:33:00,520
Just stop!

554
00:33:00,603 --> 00:33:03,272
Calm down. It's okay. Relax, it's okay.

555
00:33:04,273 --> 00:33:05,191
It's okay.

556
00:33:05,274 --> 00:33:08,444
Just breathe, Mom.
It's okay. Just breathe.

557
00:33:08,945 --> 00:33:10,363
It's gonna be okay.

558
00:33:13,783 --> 00:33:14,826
Please.

559
00:33:14,909 --> 00:33:15,868
Just breathe.

560
00:33:18,621 --> 00:33:20,415
SEE A PSYCHIATRIST BEFORE A SURGEON

561
00:33:20,498 --> 00:33:21,541
JUST BAN HER ALREADY.

562
00:33:21,624 --> 00:33:23,418
YOU'RE AN EYESORE, OLD WOMAN, SCREW OFF

563
00:33:25,962 --> 00:33:30,466
SHUT UP, PLASTIC SURGERY MONSTERS
I'LL KILL YOU, UGLY FREAKS

564
00:33:34,345 --> 00:33:36,597
BAN HER FROM HERE TOO

565
00:33:36,681 --> 00:33:38,516
SHE HAS NOWHERE ELSE TO BE. PATHETIC.

566
00:33:41,269 --> 00:33:42,311
WHO CARES ABOUT HER?

567
00:33:42,395 --> 00:33:44,439
I'M OBSESSED WITH NUMATA
ANYONE KNOW ANYTHING?

568
00:33:44,522 --> 00:33:45,982
#FIND_FUMI_NUMATA

569
00:33:49,402 --> 00:33:51,362
THE BEST PLACE TO HIDE A LEAF IS A FOREST

570
00:33:51,446 --> 00:33:52,697
I LIKE HER FACE.

571
00:33:52,780 --> 00:33:54,073
SHE HAS A CRINGEY FAN LOL.

572
00:34:01,581 --> 00:34:02,999
Numata?

573
00:34:03,666 --> 00:34:05,168
<i>I'm Dr. Tanuma.</i>

574
00:34:30,818 --> 00:34:32,945
Hi. Oh, thanks.

575
00:34:34,363 --> 00:34:36,449
Heard you had a rough night.

576
00:34:37,158 --> 00:34:39,118
Well, she's still an alcoholic.

577
00:34:41,204 --> 00:34:43,498
- I'm surprised though.
- Look at this view.

578
00:34:43,581 --> 00:34:46,667
I never thought you'd be
so committed to caring for your mother.

579
00:34:47,543 --> 00:34:49,712
I've only ever heard you
complain about her.

580
00:34:54,967 --> 00:34:56,135
You know…

581
00:34:58,846 --> 00:35:01,557
I always thought she hated me
my whole life.

582
00:35:03,226 --> 00:35:06,020
She couldn't even bring herself
to hold my hand.

583
00:35:06,646 --> 00:35:08,147
She'd say things like,

584
00:35:08,773 --> 00:35:11,567
"If a hostess smells like kids,
her career is over."

585
00:35:11,651 --> 00:35:12,944
For real?

586
00:35:13,027 --> 00:35:15,113
She never seemed
like such a toxic parent though.

587
00:35:15,196 --> 00:35:17,990
As a kid,
it was a pretty hurtful thing to hear.

588
00:35:19,617 --> 00:35:20,910
Still though.

589
00:35:20,993 --> 00:35:24,622
Look at you now,
still looking out for her after all that.

590
00:35:25,289 --> 00:35:26,958
I had to look out for Takeru.

591
00:35:28,584 --> 00:35:29,794
Besides,

592
00:35:30,545 --> 00:35:31,796
yeah, she may be flawed,

593
00:35:31,879 --> 00:35:33,714
but she's the only
actual relative I've got.

594
00:35:39,720 --> 00:35:40,930
While I'm here,

595
00:35:41,430 --> 00:35:43,599
can I ask you a question?

596
00:35:43,683 --> 00:35:44,517
Yeah?

597
00:35:47,145 --> 00:35:48,563
Who's that guy? There?

598
00:35:48,646 --> 00:35:49,689
Him?

599
00:35:50,523 --> 00:35:51,440
That's right.

600
00:35:51,941 --> 00:35:52,900
That's Macky.

601
00:35:52,984 --> 00:35:54,152
He's

602
00:35:55,361 --> 00:35:56,237
a moocher.

603
00:35:56,863 --> 00:35:58,489
- A moocher?
- That's right.

604
00:35:58,573 --> 00:36:00,741
- He mooches off you?
- Yeah.

605
00:36:01,617 --> 00:36:02,577
He lives with you?

606
00:36:02,660 --> 00:36:04,245
He doesn't have anywhere to go.

607
00:36:05,413 --> 00:36:08,332
Although, I guess he did kind of move in.

608
00:36:08,833 --> 00:36:09,917
Mm.

609
00:36:11,210 --> 00:36:12,795
- What now?
- Mm-mm.

610
00:36:12,879 --> 00:36:14,046
What?

611
00:36:15,840 --> 00:36:17,008
Hello.

612
00:36:20,261 --> 00:36:22,638
- How can I assist you?
- Is Dr. Tanuma in?

613
00:36:23,264 --> 00:36:24,557
I need to see her.

614
00:36:25,516 --> 00:36:27,393
- Uh…
- Did you hear me?

615
00:36:27,476 --> 00:36:29,187
Go get Dr. Tanuma.

616
00:36:32,231 --> 00:36:35,151
Excuse me, Director.
You're urgently needed up front.

617
00:36:35,651 --> 00:36:37,612
Get Tanuma right now!

618
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:43,701
Thank you for waiting.

619
00:36:45,161 --> 00:36:47,038
I'm Dr. Tohyama, the director.

620
00:36:47,538 --> 00:36:51,125
I'm very sorry,
but Dr. Tanuma is off today.

621
00:36:51,626 --> 00:36:53,294
She has a family matter to attend to.

622
00:36:55,004 --> 00:36:56,714
You mean Numata, right?

623
00:36:57,632 --> 00:36:58,549
What?

624
00:37:04,597 --> 00:37:06,098
Fumi Numata.

625
00:37:07,141 --> 00:37:08,017
That's her.

626
00:37:10,144 --> 00:37:11,520
Hmm.

627
00:37:11,604 --> 00:37:15,233
I guess, um,
I can see a resemblance to Dr. Tanuma.

628
00:37:15,316 --> 00:37:16,859
Don't treat me like a kid.

629
00:37:16,943 --> 00:37:20,571
Do you think it's okay for someone
like her to work under an alias?

630
00:37:20,655 --> 00:37:23,783
Isn't that a violation
of the Medical Practitioners' Act?

631
00:37:24,367 --> 00:37:25,701
What are you getting at?

632
00:37:25,785 --> 00:37:26,953
Nothing.

633
00:37:28,579 --> 00:37:29,956
All I want

634
00:37:30,039 --> 00:37:32,792
is for her to do my surgery tomorrow
like we'd discussed.

635
00:37:33,376 --> 00:37:35,211
So make sure she's here on time.

636
00:37:35,294 --> 00:37:37,255
You tell her no more excuses.

637
00:37:37,338 --> 00:37:39,590
She has to do my surgery tomorrow. Got it?

638
00:37:47,974 --> 00:37:50,643
Oh. Fumi, you're back.

639
00:37:51,310 --> 00:37:52,645
For my laundry.

640
00:37:52,728 --> 00:37:53,646
Oh.

641
00:37:58,484 --> 00:38:00,403
- Hey, Takashi.
- Yeah?

642
00:38:04,156 --> 00:38:05,241
Uh…

643
00:38:12,665 --> 00:38:14,000
It's about my…

644
00:38:16,252 --> 00:38:17,461
How do I say this?

645
00:38:17,545 --> 00:38:18,462
Hmm?

646
00:38:19,755 --> 00:38:21,632
My real father.

647
00:38:22,341 --> 00:38:24,260
Do you know anything about him?

648
00:38:25,845 --> 00:38:26,887
Uh…

649
00:38:27,680 --> 00:38:30,641
Mom never told me
anything at all about him.

650
00:38:31,142 --> 00:38:33,311
I don't even know if he's alive or dead.

651
00:38:34,770 --> 00:38:35,730
Oh.

652
00:38:36,230 --> 00:38:38,357
Well, to be honest, I don't know either.

653
00:38:40,026 --> 00:38:42,278
If I ask about him, she gets mad.

654
00:38:43,112 --> 00:38:44,739
- I see.
- Hmm.

655
00:38:48,326 --> 00:38:50,578
- Mind if I use an ashtray?
- Go ahead.

656
00:39:03,382 --> 00:39:07,053
But from what I do know,
she was really hurt by him.

657
00:39:07,553 --> 00:39:09,430
- Huh?
- I'm not gonna lie.

658
00:39:09,513 --> 00:39:11,682
I was worried
that even after all these years,

659
00:39:11,766 --> 00:39:12,975
she still wasn't over it.

660
00:39:15,561 --> 00:39:18,522
Maybe that's why
she ended up an alcoholic.

661
00:39:26,113 --> 00:39:28,324
- Good work.
- Thank you so much.

662
00:39:28,407 --> 00:39:30,076
- This way to the dressing room.
- Thank you.

663
00:39:30,785 --> 00:39:31,619
Nice job.

664
00:39:31,702 --> 00:39:33,788
- Great work. Thank you so much.
- No, thank you.

665
00:39:34,288 --> 00:39:35,456
Amazing job.

666
00:39:39,251 --> 00:39:40,544
Hey, well done.

667
00:39:44,090 --> 00:39:45,341
Hi, Dad, good morning.

668
00:39:45,424 --> 00:39:46,509
<i>Hey, so…</i>

669
00:39:46,592 --> 00:39:50,388
My team needed me for a meeting,
so I'm back in Japan.

670
00:39:50,471 --> 00:39:52,098
I see.

671
00:39:52,181 --> 00:39:54,433
Dad, you should have told me sooner.

672
00:39:54,517 --> 00:39:57,395
<i>Well, I have to fly right back tomorrow.</i>

673
00:39:58,187 --> 00:39:59,105
<i>But I called you</i>

674
00:39:59,188 --> 00:40:03,776
because I wanted to talk to you
about Tokyo's Global Beauty Hub project.

675
00:40:04,735 --> 00:40:06,821
I've decided to join the campaign.

676
00:40:08,614 --> 00:40:11,158
<i>I've been wanting to speak out</i>
<i>about the rise of chains</i>

677
00:40:11,242 --> 00:40:13,411
<i>in the plastic surgery industry.</i>

678
00:40:14,745 --> 00:40:17,081
Well, this is the perfect opportunity
to do so.

679
00:40:17,832 --> 00:40:19,458
Oh!

680
00:40:19,542 --> 00:40:20,543
Well, that's great.

681
00:40:21,210 --> 00:40:24,505
I was actually just about to call you
to discuss all that.

682
00:40:24,588 --> 00:40:25,840
Don't worry.

683
00:40:26,465 --> 00:40:28,092
I know what's on your mind, Rin.

684
00:40:28,592 --> 00:40:29,844
No need to tell me.

685
00:40:31,303 --> 00:40:33,431
I'm very much aware of how you feel.

686
00:40:50,239 --> 00:40:52,658
Dr. Rin, great job today.

687
00:40:53,159 --> 00:40:54,201
Do you have a second?

688
00:40:54,869 --> 00:40:56,620
A new project already?

689
00:40:56,704 --> 00:40:57,788
Yes.

690
00:40:57,872 --> 00:41:01,208
The show had a resurgence in popularity
ever since Ms. Yuriko died.

691
00:41:01,750 --> 00:41:05,838
So the network is insisting that
we jump right on another program with you.

692
00:41:08,924 --> 00:41:09,800
Here's our pitch.

693
00:41:09,884 --> 00:41:12,178
BEAUTY REVOLUTION
REIWA EDITION

694
00:41:15,723 --> 00:41:16,682
Are you serious?

695
00:41:18,392 --> 00:41:21,729
Can you let us know
if we can aim for an October release?

696
00:41:23,397 --> 00:41:25,107
DREAM COLLAB FOR THE HANDS OF GOD!

697
00:41:27,443 --> 00:41:28,652
The chairman's doing it?

698
00:41:28,736 --> 00:41:31,697
Well, of course.
He's the most popular part of it.

699
00:41:32,490 --> 00:41:35,993
Well, I mean, with the two of you both
acting as the Hand of God,

700
00:41:36,076 --> 00:41:38,454
just think of the impact in our ratings.

701
00:41:41,207 --> 00:41:42,208
So?

702
00:41:43,167 --> 00:41:44,001
I'm sorry.

703
00:41:44,585 --> 00:41:47,171
My schedule is already completely full,
I'm afraid.

704
00:41:47,254 --> 00:41:48,506
There's no time.

705
00:42:07,358 --> 00:42:08,442
Takashina.

706
00:42:10,361 --> 00:42:13,239
We need… to make a stop.

707
00:42:13,322 --> 00:42:14,990
All right. Where would you like to go?

708
00:42:16,617 --> 00:42:18,077
I'm going to see Dad.

709
00:42:20,788 --> 00:42:24,208
I'm not letting him
push me around anymore.

710
00:43:10,963 --> 00:43:13,257
SNACK BAR ITTENBARI

711
00:43:20,973 --> 00:43:22,099
TOHYAMA CLINIC

712
00:43:24,268 --> 00:43:25,311
Hello?

713
00:43:26,812 --> 00:43:28,564
I'm calling about Ms. Itai.

714
00:43:29,773 --> 00:43:32,526
I've decided
to cancel her surgery tomorrow.

715
00:43:34,445 --> 00:43:36,322
Well, she isn't going to like that.

716
00:43:36,405 --> 00:43:40,242
My plan is to offer her a cash settlement
in exchange for her silence.

717
00:43:41,452 --> 00:43:43,704
So you're hoping
you can just buy her off, huh?

718
00:43:43,787 --> 00:43:47,082
You're the reason
we're in this mess in the first place.

719
00:43:48,500 --> 00:43:51,670
I decided that she's too risky of a client
for us to take on.

720
00:43:52,546 --> 00:43:55,966
If our only concern was a complaint,
that would be perfectly manageable.

721
00:43:56,050 --> 00:43:59,511
However, she has a history
with the police.

722
00:43:59,595 --> 00:44:00,429
The cops?

723
00:44:00,512 --> 00:44:02,890
She went through
a nasty divorce a few years ago.

724
00:44:03,599 --> 00:44:08,604
Seems she filed for custody of her son,
but lost her case in court.

725
00:44:09,313 --> 00:44:11,357
<i>She couldn't let the matter go</i>

726
00:44:11,857 --> 00:44:15,486
<i>and took it upon herself to harass those</i>
<i>who were involved in the case.</i>

727
00:44:15,986 --> 00:44:17,279
I see.

728
00:44:17,363 --> 00:44:21,992
She has also figured out
who you really are, Dr. Numata.

729
00:44:22,618 --> 00:44:23,452
Has she really?

730
00:44:24,828 --> 00:44:28,248
<i>If we don't stop her now,</i>
<i>she'll use this information as leverage.</i>

731
00:44:30,334 --> 00:44:32,544
<i>The clinic is at a critical crossroad.</i>

732
00:44:34,380 --> 00:44:36,256
We can't afford another scandal.

733
00:44:37,508 --> 00:44:38,676
I'll handle this.

734
00:44:39,218 --> 00:44:40,761
I'll talk to her tomorrow.

735
00:44:43,138 --> 00:44:46,684
Oh, and according to our PR department,

736
00:44:47,434 --> 00:44:50,729
the backlash against you
is even more rampant than ever.

737
00:44:50,813 --> 00:44:52,398
So working under your real name

738
00:44:53,816 --> 00:44:55,401
might be a little bit tricky.

739
00:45:04,076 --> 00:45:04,910
Here.

740
00:45:06,578 --> 00:45:07,579
And there.

741
00:45:07,663 --> 00:45:10,457
Takeru. Visiting hours are over.

742
00:45:11,208 --> 00:45:13,085
Why do you get to stay over?

743
00:45:13,168 --> 00:45:14,753
- What?
- I wanna stay.

744
00:45:15,838 --> 00:45:18,173
Can I have many visitors overnight?

745
00:45:18,257 --> 00:45:20,843
One person.
Only one is allowed to stay at a time.

746
00:45:22,052 --> 00:45:23,595
Ask that Dr. Tojo.

747
00:45:24,096 --> 00:45:26,598
He's obsessed with you.
He'll let us both stay.

748
00:45:27,599 --> 00:45:29,518
Dr. Tojo?

749
00:45:32,730 --> 00:45:35,190
- Ah!
- Come on. Stop that.

750
00:45:35,274 --> 00:45:37,151
Come on, it's obvious.

751
00:45:39,194 --> 00:45:41,905
Okay, you can stay.

752
00:45:41,989 --> 00:45:43,741
Lights off.

753
00:45:43,824 --> 00:45:45,784
Hey, come closer.

754
00:45:45,868 --> 00:45:48,162
You don't have to
push the beds that close.

755
00:45:48,245 --> 00:45:49,663
Good night, Ms. Taeko.

756
00:45:50,581 --> 00:45:51,874
Good night.

757
00:45:54,793 --> 00:45:56,545
Uh, if I may…

758
00:45:57,296 --> 00:45:58,172
Hmm?

759
00:45:59,423 --> 00:46:01,049
Isn't your mom…

760
00:46:02,968 --> 00:46:05,012
worried about where you two are?

761
00:46:05,095 --> 00:46:06,680
What?

762
00:46:09,057 --> 00:46:10,392
That's a good question.

763
00:46:10,476 --> 00:46:12,728
She's not really that type of person.

764
00:46:12,811 --> 00:46:13,645
Mm.

765
00:46:14,146 --> 00:46:15,731
Oh, I see.

766
00:46:18,525 --> 00:46:19,777
What's she like?

767
00:46:21,904 --> 00:46:23,197
Huh?

768
00:46:23,697 --> 00:46:26,116
Hey, tell me.

769
00:46:26,617 --> 00:46:28,702
Tell me something about her.

770
00:46:34,666 --> 00:46:35,876
Well,

771
00:46:37,336 --> 00:46:38,754
to be honest…

772
00:46:42,007 --> 00:46:44,802
I hate her more than anyone in the world.

773
00:46:46,053 --> 00:46:47,221
What?

774
00:46:48,597 --> 00:46:49,598
Our mom,

775
00:46:51,058 --> 00:46:53,644
she was a hostess like you, Ms. Taeko.

776
00:46:55,771 --> 00:46:57,356
She was always drunk.

777
00:46:57,981 --> 00:46:59,608
Had tons of lovers.

778
00:47:01,443 --> 00:47:03,278
She would always

779
00:47:04,613 --> 00:47:07,282
put her own needs before anyone else's,

780
00:47:07,366 --> 00:47:08,867
including her kids.

781
00:47:10,661 --> 00:47:11,620
Yeah.

782
00:47:13,914 --> 00:47:15,582
Now, it seems that…

783
00:47:17,543 --> 00:47:18,919
Seems that what?

784
00:47:21,547 --> 00:47:23,423
I'm finally aware that…

785
00:47:26,510 --> 00:47:28,512
life wasn't easy for her.

786
00:47:31,807 --> 00:47:35,644
I'll admit
I've been avoiding talking to her

787
00:47:37,020 --> 00:47:39,147
about how she hurt me.

788
00:47:41,859 --> 00:47:42,985
And now…

789
00:47:45,654 --> 00:47:48,532
I feel like I should have
just listened to her.

790
00:47:50,742 --> 00:47:53,787
I should have asked her to tell me
what she went through.

791
00:47:56,707 --> 00:47:57,583
But…

792
00:47:59,209 --> 00:48:01,128
I missed my chance.

793
00:48:21,273 --> 00:48:22,858
That's not true.

794
00:48:25,652 --> 00:48:28,322
If you're this aware of your feelings…

795
00:48:30,991 --> 00:48:32,993
and I think your mother is too…

796
00:48:37,164 --> 00:48:38,874
and she's lucky to have you.

797
00:48:44,796 --> 00:48:45,756
Hmm.

798
00:48:47,132 --> 00:48:48,175
It's okay.

799
00:48:49,676 --> 00:48:50,761
It's okay.

800
00:48:52,512 --> 00:48:54,681
It's gonna be okay. It's fine.

801
00:48:58,435 --> 00:48:59,645
Someday…

802
00:49:03,357 --> 00:49:05,192
you'll understand each other.

803
00:50:05,085 --> 00:50:07,421
I'm not… I'm not ready to see him.

804
00:50:07,504 --> 00:50:09,589
No, I can't! No!

805
00:50:20,308 --> 00:50:23,061
No! Tomo can't see me like this!

806
00:51:35,175 --> 00:51:36,718
<i>Yes, Tohyama speaking.</i>

807
00:51:37,302 --> 00:51:39,179
<i>Hello, sorry to call so late.</i>

808
00:51:39,262 --> 00:51:41,681
<i>This is Hamaguchi, the TV director.</i>

809
00:51:42,849 --> 00:51:46,770
<i>Um, I just wanted to talk about</i>
<i>the new project.</i>

810
00:51:47,813 --> 00:51:50,357
<i>Dr. Rin has declined.</i>

811
00:51:50,982 --> 00:51:53,902
I see. That's too bad.

812
00:51:55,237 --> 00:52:00,700
In fact, I was very much looking forward
to watching her in action.

813
00:52:01,451 --> 00:52:02,452
<i>Same.</i>

814
00:52:03,495 --> 00:52:07,707
<i>Well, it seems she's really set</i>
<i>on appearing on her own.</i>

815
00:52:09,835 --> 00:52:11,461
<i>I'm very sorry.</i>

816
00:52:11,545 --> 00:52:14,840
<i>We reached out to you, assuming</i>
<i>she'd want a collaboration, but…</i>

817
00:52:23,598 --> 00:52:25,642
Please wait in here for the doctor.

818
00:52:26,685 --> 00:52:31,356
I'll leave it to you, Doctor, to decide
what the final settlement will be.

819
00:52:32,482 --> 00:52:34,818
Excuse me, Director. A moment?

820
00:52:37,028 --> 00:52:37,863
Yes, what is it?

821
00:52:38,572 --> 00:52:40,115
Sorry for interrupting.

822
00:52:42,784 --> 00:52:45,370
It's about Ms. Itai.

823
00:52:47,372 --> 00:52:50,876
I'd like… to take this one on myself.

824
00:52:52,794 --> 00:52:53,628
Why?

825
00:52:56,965 --> 00:52:59,718
Don't you need to scrub up?
Isn't the surgery soon?

826
00:53:00,218 --> 00:53:03,889
Before we proceed, the director would like
to have a word with you.

827
00:53:05,307 --> 00:53:10,103
I don't believe that a cash settlement
will satisfy her.

828
00:53:10,187 --> 00:53:11,813
She's unwell.

829
00:53:11,897 --> 00:53:13,899
She could have surgery after surgery.

830
00:53:13,982 --> 00:53:15,483
She will never be satisfied.

831
00:53:15,567 --> 00:53:16,484
Exactly.

832
00:53:17,694 --> 00:53:18,945
Ideally,

833
00:53:19,863 --> 00:53:23,742
you should have talked to her
about this much earlier.

834
00:53:25,118 --> 00:53:26,119
So I

835
00:53:27,579 --> 00:53:29,206
wanna make sure I understand.

836
00:53:31,416 --> 00:53:34,044
I wanna know
what she's actually struggling with.

837
00:53:35,253 --> 00:53:36,880
I wanna hear her out.

838
00:53:38,924 --> 00:53:40,133
As a doctor.

839
00:53:42,344 --> 00:53:44,304
You asked me once if I felt ready.

840
00:53:46,932 --> 00:53:49,559
Ready to support our patients
who want to change their appearance.

841
00:53:52,187 --> 00:53:53,730
I need to do this.

842
00:53:56,024 --> 00:53:57,234
To hear her out.

843
00:53:58,526 --> 00:53:59,736
Please, Director.

844
00:54:03,615 --> 00:54:04,866
Excuse me.

845
00:54:06,576 --> 00:54:07,577
Director.

846
00:54:12,165 --> 00:54:13,708
The chairman is out front.

847
00:54:18,213 --> 00:54:19,798
<i>You want to get surgery?</i>

848
00:54:20,632 --> 00:54:23,551
I know it's very sudden,
but I'd like you to do it.

849
00:54:26,012 --> 00:54:27,681
What made you want this now?

850
00:54:27,764 --> 00:54:31,059
Well, I looked
for a suitable doctor in Dubai,

851
00:54:31,142 --> 00:54:32,894
but I just couldn't find one.

852
00:54:33,478 --> 00:54:35,313
It's a fairly big surgery.

853
00:54:35,397 --> 00:54:38,775
So I figured, why not ask
the most trustworthy doctor.

854
00:54:39,776 --> 00:54:40,652
What kind of surgery?

855
00:54:43,446 --> 00:54:45,031
Do you remember Ms. Yuriko?

856
00:54:45,615 --> 00:54:47,575
I'd like the same procedure.

857
00:54:48,493 --> 00:54:49,828
I'd like a facelift.

858
00:55:00,797 --> 00:55:02,215
You okay?

859
00:55:08,054 --> 00:55:11,099
Unfortunately, our anesthesiologist
isn't in today, so--

860
00:55:11,182 --> 00:55:12,976
I've already reached out to Taki.

861
00:55:13,977 --> 00:55:15,395
He's on his way.

862
00:55:16,229 --> 00:55:17,605
Oh, one other thing.

863
00:55:17,689 --> 00:55:22,068
I'd like to film the surgery
and air it on my channel.

864
00:55:23,194 --> 00:55:26,156
The publicity will be good
for the Global Beauty Hub.

865
00:55:36,374 --> 00:55:37,959
I'd like to apologize

866
00:55:39,669 --> 00:55:41,588
for lying about my identity.

867
00:55:55,352 --> 00:55:56,936
DR. TANUMA

868
00:55:57,020 --> 00:55:58,021
If

869
00:55:59,564 --> 00:56:02,609
you're willing
to give me a second chance, Ms. Itai,

870
00:56:03,693 --> 00:56:05,320
I swear I'll do my best.

871
00:56:08,782 --> 00:56:10,992
How can I trust anything you have to say?

872
00:56:14,412 --> 00:56:15,497
You can't.

873
00:56:17,082 --> 00:56:19,793
But I would still like to help you
however I can.

874
00:56:23,213 --> 00:56:24,589
I will hear you out…

875
00:56:26,549 --> 00:56:29,177
as a surgeon and without any judgment,

876
00:56:30,887 --> 00:56:33,515
until you walk out of here
totally satisfied.

877
00:56:34,349 --> 00:56:35,266
Tell me.

878
00:56:49,322 --> 00:56:50,949
Can I really trust you?

879
00:57:14,848 --> 00:57:15,682
What is it?

880
00:57:17,016 --> 00:57:19,644
I heard a talented doctor
joined us recently.

881
00:57:20,770 --> 00:57:22,439
Ms. Tanuma.

882
00:57:24,524 --> 00:57:27,777
You've got great fingers for surgery.

883
00:57:29,988 --> 00:57:31,781
If only we were all so lucky.

884
00:57:47,172 --> 00:57:48,006
Director.

885
00:57:53,261 --> 00:57:54,220
It's okay.

886
00:58:09,777 --> 00:58:10,820
Lights.

887
00:58:11,654 --> 00:58:13,573
- Administering anesthesia.
- Right.

888
00:58:27,295 --> 00:58:28,838
- <i>We'll begin the lip lift.</i>
<i>- Right.</i>

889
00:58:29,422 --> 00:58:30,715
- Anesthesia.
- Here.

890
00:58:39,974 --> 00:58:42,393
Director, the anesthesia
has been administered.

891
00:58:45,438 --> 00:58:46,356
Scalpel.

892
00:58:46,439 --> 00:58:47,357
Yes.

893
00:59:07,669 --> 00:59:11,506
Director, should we wait
until Dr. Numata is finished?

894
00:59:28,690 --> 00:59:30,441
Dr. Numata, a moment?

895
00:59:31,067 --> 00:59:34,028
- Okay. Continue hemostasis.
- Understood.

896
00:59:34,112 --> 00:59:36,197
- Close the door.
- Yes.

897
00:59:36,698 --> 00:59:37,824
Excuse me.

898
00:59:47,417 --> 00:59:48,543
I understand.

899
00:59:53,256 --> 00:59:54,382
- New gauze.
- Yes.

900
01:00:06,978 --> 01:00:07,979
<i>It's okay.</i>

901
01:00:32,712 --> 01:00:34,005
All right.

902
01:00:35,089 --> 01:00:36,674
- Let's begin.
- Okay.

903
01:01:34,607 --> 01:01:36,150
Here we go. Hold on tight!

904
01:01:36,234 --> 01:01:39,612
It's like we're off to the races!

905
01:01:40,822 --> 01:01:43,157
So what do you think of
my driving skills, huh?

906
01:01:43,241 --> 01:01:45,785
You win best driver ever!

907
01:01:47,787 --> 01:01:49,914
Can you imagine
if they actually end up together?

908
01:01:49,997 --> 01:01:52,333
Don't be so weird.

909
01:01:53,793 --> 01:01:54,836
It's all so weird.

910
01:01:54,919 --> 01:01:55,837
Hmm?

911
01:01:57,255 --> 01:01:59,966
She lost her memories,
but she's still Mom.

912
01:02:01,259 --> 01:02:02,969
You're being so nice to her.

913
01:02:05,722 --> 01:02:07,932
Well, yeah. Doctors always try to be nice.

914
01:02:08,599 --> 01:02:09,475
You know,

915
01:02:10,643 --> 01:02:12,770
this whole situation might not be so bad.

916
01:02:12,854 --> 01:02:13,813
How so?

917
01:02:15,106 --> 01:02:18,192
When you think about it,
we'd all be happier if we could forget.

918
01:02:26,451 --> 01:02:29,495
DIRECTOR

919
01:02:35,501 --> 01:02:36,502
Hello.

920
01:02:36,586 --> 01:02:38,755
Hi! It's nice to finally meet you.
I've heard so much.

921
01:02:39,380 --> 01:02:40,381
Come in.

922
01:02:40,465 --> 01:02:42,175
Oh, thank you.

923
01:02:46,888 --> 01:02:47,972
Rin.

924
01:02:48,931 --> 01:02:50,016
Whoa!

925
01:02:50,099 --> 01:02:52,435
Thank you for coming all this way.

926
01:02:52,518 --> 01:02:53,770
It's my pleasure.

927
01:02:54,645 --> 01:02:57,565
Since we've both made it out
of a tough situation,

928
01:02:57,648 --> 01:03:00,443
I thought we could celebrate
with a home-cooked meal.

929
01:03:01,027 --> 01:03:02,987
We still don't know
how Ms. Itai will feel.

930
01:03:04,155 --> 01:03:06,324
We haven't gotten any complaints yet,

931
01:03:07,241 --> 01:03:10,661
which leads me to think
she was satisfied with her surgery.

932
01:03:10,745 --> 01:03:12,205
I hope so.

933
01:03:13,581 --> 01:03:16,042
Wow, your home is so nice.

934
01:03:16,125 --> 01:03:16,959
Thank you.

935
01:03:17,752 --> 01:03:20,797
If you keep working for us for a year,
you could get a place like this.

936
01:03:21,380 --> 01:03:22,882
Just like that, huh?

937
01:03:23,591 --> 01:03:25,343
Would you mind if I look around?

938
01:03:25,843 --> 01:03:26,928
By all means.

939
01:03:27,762 --> 01:03:29,305
Dinner is ready. It'll get cold.

940
01:03:29,889 --> 01:03:33,643
Ah, in that case,
let's save the tour for later.

941
01:03:34,310 --> 01:03:38,022
You never want to annoy
the person who's handling your food.

942
01:03:39,190 --> 01:03:41,692
Ms. Taeko, I'm off.

943
01:03:46,989 --> 01:03:47,865
Good night.

944
01:03:50,952 --> 01:03:52,078
Sleep well.

945
01:03:54,121 --> 01:03:55,331
<i>What?</i>

946
01:03:55,414 --> 01:03:56,666
You're crazy.

947
01:03:56,749 --> 01:03:58,251
Game Boy is in black and white.

948
01:03:58,334 --> 01:03:59,710
No, it's in color.

949
01:03:59,794 --> 01:04:02,630
See? I told you yours was broken.

950
01:04:02,713 --> 01:04:05,591
No way, I swear. I got it for my birthday.

951
01:04:05,675 --> 01:04:07,552
But then why was mine in black and white?

952
01:04:08,636 --> 01:04:11,389
Oh no. Does that mean I'm officially old?

953
01:04:13,808 --> 01:04:14,725
Good lord.

954
01:04:15,226 --> 01:04:16,811
OKURA
URGENT! CAN WE TALK NOW?

955
01:04:16,894 --> 01:04:19,939
Oh. So sorry.
Um, do you mind if I make a call?

956
01:04:20,022 --> 01:04:21,941
Not at all. Use the balcony.

957
01:04:22,024 --> 01:04:23,734
- Thank you so much.
- Of course.

958
01:04:27,446 --> 01:04:28,447
<i>Hello?</i>

959
01:04:28,531 --> 01:04:32,285
I found out who's been adding fuel
to the fire against you online.

960
01:04:32,785 --> 01:04:33,786
I'm listening.

961
01:04:34,537 --> 01:04:38,291
<i>It's some guy named Takashina.</i>
<i>He's from the Tohyama Clinic.</i>

962
01:04:38,374 --> 01:04:39,542
<i>Used to be a detective.</i>

963
01:04:41,043 --> 01:04:45,131
<i>Seems like he's been leaking info on you</i>
<i>to major influencers</i>

964
01:04:45,214 --> 01:04:47,884
<i>and spreading rumors to keep you trending.</i>

965
01:04:48,843 --> 01:04:50,094
<i>But the whole thing is weird</i>

966
01:04:50,177 --> 01:04:54,932
'cause, I mean, you've been working there
for a while now, right?

967
01:04:55,516 --> 01:04:59,478
So what exactly is the point of
stirring all of this up against you now?
